UID:7tt1tdlqrg12lh8i8oebub0epo@google.com
CREATED:20140929T153727Z
DESCRIPTION:The San Marco Preservation Society invites you to the “Farm to 
 San Marco Dinner” at Whatley Park on Saturday\, October 25th. This five cou
 rse\, open air\, farm to table dinner\, pairs local brewers/distillers with
  several of Jacksonville’s best restaurants\, creating dishes featuring loc
 al ingredients\, making each course one of a kind and uniquely Jacksonville
 . San Marco Preservation Society\, in partnership with Slow Food First Coas
 t and GastroJax Inc. and with the support of Champion Brands\, Inc.\, bring
  this special dining experience to life. All proceeds from this dinner bene
 fit North Florida School of Special Education’s Berry Good Farm and Whatley
  Park improvements. \n\nCome enjoy courses prepared by Bistro Aix\, BB’s\, 
 Dig Foods\, Ribault Bakery\, and Berry Good Farms. Various parings include 
 Intuition\, Aardwolf\, and Veterans United Beers and cocktails from Grape a
 nd Grain Exchange using local spirits from St. Augustine and Palm Ridge Dis
 tilleries. Meet the brewers\, distillers\, chefs\, and farmers themselves a
 s they discuss each memorable course with you. Tickets are expected to sell
  out quickly for this amazing event.Tickets go on sale Sept. 15 on the San 
 Marco Preservation website.\n\nCost for San Marco Preservation Members is $
 125\, Non-members $150. If you are not yet a member\, sign-up now to get th
 e discounted rate. See you October 25th when the best local ingredients\, f
