UID:jdloknhvpds3c6140d4g7qm514@google.com
CREATED:20150305T215417Z
DESCRIPTION:The Armada FC have teamed up local JAX concert promoters Orange
  Peel Entertainment to host the first annual CAN-DOO FEST to celebrate the 
 Armada’s first regular season match in the North American Soccer on Saturda
 y\, April 4th against FC Edmonton. \n\nNational touring band O.A.R. will he
 adline the huge pre-match party event at Metropolitan Park across from Ever
 Bank Field on Saturday\, April 4th from noon to 7:00pm ahead of the Armada’
 s opening regular-season match up against the Eddies which kicks off at 7:3
 0 p.m.\n\n“This is a big day for the Jacksonville sports and entertainment 
 scene\,” said Armada president Steve Livingstone. “By partnering with Orang
 e Peel Entertainment as a presenting co-sponsor alongside Community First C
 redit Union\, we have designated this huge music festival as our official p
 re-match party venue for our NASL kickoff and will provide ALL Armada FC se
 ason ticket owners with a complimentary admission to the CAN-DOO FEST as pa
 rt of their match ticket courtesy of Community First.\n\n“Non-season ticket
  owners will also be able to get in on the event headlined by O.A.R. with a
  combined match/concert ticket starting at just $35 while limited supplies 
 last. Combining both major events will not only provide great value with en
 try to the entire CAN-DOO FEST as well as a ticket to the Armada FC v FC Ed
 monton match at EverBank Field immediately following the festival at 7:30pm
 \, it will also create a huge and memorable occasion for the city of Jackso
 nville on Easter Weekend.”\n\nCAN-DOO FEST will be a day-long canned craft 
 beer festival featuring canned beers from Oskar Blues\, Veterans United\, N
 ew Belgium\, Sierra Nevada\, Sam Adams\, and Miller-Coors breweries. The li
 ve music starts at 1:00pm with musical acts including Tishamingo and The Co
 rbitt Brothers….as well as headliner O.A.R. Following the concert\, fans wi
 ll gather for the Armada FC’s March to the Match which will leave Met Park 
 at 7:00 p.m.\, crossing over Gator Bowl Blvd to EverBank Field in time for 
 the 7:30 p.m. match kickoff.\n\nA successful recording and touring band for
  more than a decade\, O.A.R. is renowned for an intense\, vibrant live show
  and the communal feeling it shares with its fans. Since their formation in
  1996\, O.A.R. (singer Marc Roberge\, drummer Chris Culos\, guitarist Richa
 rd On\, bassist Benj Gershman and saxophonist Jerry DePizzo) has logged mil
 lions of miles on the road and released eight studio albums\, spawning such
  hit singles as “Shattered\,” “Heaven\,” “Love and Memories” and “Peace.”\n
 \nLocal event promoter Orange Peel Entertainment\, headed by founder and pr
 incipal Billy Catlin\, have partnered with the Armada to make downtown the 
 ultimate destination for music and sports on April 4. \n\n“There will be an
  incredible buzz in and around Downtown with this game and our kickoff even
 t\,” said Catlin\, who organized the big Florida Georgia Line TAILGATE at l
 ast year’s Georgia Florida Classic. “Mixing amazing craft beers with music 
 is always a great fit. Adding the Armada’s first regular season match is th
 e icing on the cake for a package that will attract thousands to downtown J
 acksonville.”\n\nTickets to Armada FC CAN-DOO KICKOFF FEST and the Jacksonv
 ille Armada match will be bundled and go on sale\, starting at $35\, on Mon
 day March 9th at 9:00 a.m.\, at www.armadafc.com\,  www.candoofest.com or b
 y calling 844-2-ARMADA.
LAST-MODIFIED:20150310T200323Z
LOCATION:Metropolitan Park\, 4110 Gator Bowl Boulevard\, Jacksonville\, FL 
 32202\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:FESTIVAL: Can-Doo Fest
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
