CREATED:20200613T112622Z
DESCRIPTION:A VERY Special Visitor!\n\nJohn Burnam is in the taproom TODAY 
 at 2PM for a brief visit!\n\nCome in for a howdy-do!\n\nJohn Burnam was a V
 ietnam-era dog handler and assisted us in naming our Scout Dog 44 Amber Ale
 !\n\nMr Burnam wrote many books\, including "Canine Warrior\," AND he is al
 so the founder of the National US Military Working Dogs Teams monument at L
 ackland AFB!\n\nIf you'd like to learn more about US military dogs\, come p
 ick up a SIGNED copy of John Burnam's Book\, "Canine Warrior: How a Vietnam
  Scout Dog Inspired a National Monument!" \n\nFor our Scout Dog 44 Amber Al
 e\, it's more like "How a National Monument inspired a Beer!" \n\nScout Dog
  44 is named for SSGT Robert W Hartsock\, the only dog handler to receive t
 he Congressional Medal of Honor (Vietnam). \n\nMr Hartsock was in Infantry 
 Platoon 44\, aka Scout Dog\, hence the Scout Dog 44 name.\n\nOur Scout Dog 
 44 Amber Ale honors ALL working dogs and their handlers - MWDs\, CWD\, Poli
 ce K9s\, SARs\, Service Dogs\, etc!\n\nSigned copies of "Canine Warrior" ar
 e available at the brewery for $25 and ALL PROCEEDS go to the National US M
 ilitary Working Dogs Teams monument!\n\nWOOF! 🐕🐾❤️🐕🐾❤️🐕
LAST-MODIFIED:20200613T112622Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:John Burnam
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
